tour feature-tours
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note tours [name]: the map as an outline. The agent reaches for it before touching code, so it neither duplicates nor misses a tour that already names the area. Without a name, every tour in tours-list order, each group announced by a '== group' header line, then the tour's row (name, kind, author, step count, note) and its steps in tree order, indented by depth. With a name, only that tour and no group header. Each step row carries its index in square brackets, which is the number every step-editing command takes, a leading ! when the step is stale, (ai) for agent-authored steps and an arrow for a link. This is the agent's first command in an area: it shows what is already named before any code is read.

